 {"clause_id": "c020", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause provides for the Account to pass to the named beneficiary \"if that person is still living\" but says nothing about who takes if the beneficiary predeceases the trustee or if several beneficiaries are named. That gap, plus the deemed characterization as a \"Revocable Unwritten Trust\", is what would be construed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c021", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c022", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause limits changes and withdrawals for \"either of these Trust Account types\" to what is \"permitted by the trust instrument or court order\", but the Unwritten Trust described in the immediately preceding clause exists precisely where no written trust instrument or court order was provided. Read together with that clause, the limitation has nothing to operate on, and it also contradicts the statement there that the trustee \"may withdraw all of the funds during your lifetime\".", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c023", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c024", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c025", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The bracketed passage leaves the age of the \"minor\" to vary between eighteen and twenty-one \"depending on the jurisdiction ... and the circumstances\", and the transfer duty is triggered at majority \"or at another time determined by applicable law\". When the custodianship ends, and thus when the Bank must transfer the funds, is not fixed by the text.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.19}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c026", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bank's discretion to \"delay or refuse to give you provisional credit\" and its power to \"determine when final credit is received\" sit against Part III's Funds Availability Policy, which commits the Bank to fixed availability schedules for deposited items. Which controls when the Bank withholds provisional credit on an item that the Policy makes available is not resolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.25}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c027", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause states flatly that \"The Funds Availability Policy does not apply to items we have accepted for collection only\", but Part III's \"Non-U.S. Financial Institutions\" section, itself part of that Policy, prescribes availability for items sent for collection (generally within thirty Calendar Days, and by the third Business Day for Canadian items not sent for collection). The two cannot both be given effect for foreign collection items.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c028", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause manufactures a waiver of the customer's \"right to receive immediate notice of dishonor\" from the Bank's mere option to re-present the item (\"This means that you are waiving\"), without any separate assent or notice mechanism. Whether re-presentment effects that waiver is the construction question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.19}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c029", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Typically, the Bank will cash checks drawn on other banks for its customers who have adequate available funds\" is hedged by \"typically\" and by the undefined standard of \"adequate available funds\", so it is unclear whether any obligation to cash is created at all. The word \"typically\" is what a court would have to construe.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c030", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c031", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c032", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause reserves a seven Calendar Day notice right for all Savings and Money Market Accounts, while the sub-account provision reserving the same seven-day right adds that \"the Bank does not presently exercise this right\". Whether the Bank may in fact impose the notice requirement on savings withdrawals turns on reading the two reservations together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.19}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c033", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Repeated violations will result in the Account being closed or changed from a savings type Account to a transaction Account\" gives no number, period or standard for \"repeated\". The trigger for the mandatory consequence is therefore indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c034", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause measures excess withdrawals \"in any calendar month\", whereas the immediately preceding savings-withdrawal clause measures them by \"any monthly period (based on your statement date)\". Which period governs a Holiday Club or Club Saver Account whose statement cycle is not a calendar month is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause assures that sub-account transfers cause \"no adverse impact on the availability of the balances held in your Checking Account\", yet the same paragraph caps transfers out of the non-transaction sub-account at six per statement cycle and gives the Bank unfettered discretion over the transfer threshold. The assurance and the limitation pull against each other.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.21}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c036", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c037", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause reserves a seven Calendar Day notice right and then says \"the Bank does not presently exercise this right\", leaving open whether and with what notice the Bank could begin to exercise it. \"Does not presently exercise\" is the phrase requiring construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c038", "issues": [
   {"issue": "After five specific withholding triggers, item (f) adds \"there may be other reasons why we may be required to do so under applicable law\", a catch-all that swallows the enumerated list. Whether the list is exhaustive or merely illustrative is the classic construction question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c039", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Reporting to consumer reporting agencies is triggered where an Account \"is closed for insufficient funds activity or other negative reason\", and \"other negative reason\" has no stated limit against the single specific it follows. The scope of the reportable closures is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c040", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c041", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause excuses the Bank from sending a statement in three situations, yet the limitation-on-claims clause runs the customer's fourteen- and thirty-day reporting periods from the date \"we mailed a statement (or otherwise made it available to you)\". How the reporting deadlines operate when no statement is sent at all cannot be answered from either clause alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c042", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause states the review-and-report duty in open terms (\"promptly\", \"as soon as possible\", \"call us at once\"), while the later clause fixes fourteen Calendar Days as reasonable and thirty Calendar Days as an absolute bar. Whether the flexible standard here or the fixed periods there measure the customer's duty is a genuine question.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.21}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c043", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause deems statements and check images \"available\" as of the statement mailing date irrespective of receipt, which is the event that starts every reporting period. Whether \"available\" can be deemed to occur on mailing, particularly where the Bank never mails or the customer never receives, is what would be construed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c044", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Failure or refusal to do \"these things\" — cooperate, seek criminal and civil penalties, file reports and complaints, and give a sworn statement — is deemed a ratification of the defect in the item. The scope of the required \"cooperation\" and the deemed ratification consequence are both open to construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c045", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause sets two different periods for the same conduct: fourteen Calendar Days is agreed to be \"a reasonable amount of time ... to review your Account statement and report any errors\", but claims are barred only if not reported within thirty Calendar Days. Which period governs a customer who reports on day twenty is not stated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.34},
   {"issue": "The thirty Calendar Day bar covers \"any error, forgery or other problem relating to a matter shown on an Account statement\", while Part IV's Unauthorized Transfers section gives the customer sixty Calendar Days after the statement was mailed to report transfers he did not make. The two notice deadlines cannot both govern an unauthorized electronic debit appearing on a statement.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c046", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bank may destroy original checks \"not less than thirty (30) Calendar Days after the statement mailing date\", which is the same day the customer's thirty-Calendar-Day window to report a forgery under the preceding clause expires. Destruction of the evidence at the very moment the claim must be asserted is a tension between the two clauses.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c047", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c048", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c049", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bank may refuse a check that is not \"in a form supplied by or previously approved by the Bank\" or which is \"incompletely or defectively drawn\", with no standard for approval and no definition of defective drawing. Both phrases leave the refusal right without an ascertainable boundary.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c050", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition of \"item\" closes a long enumerated list with \"any other instruction or order for the payment, transfer or withdrawal of funds\", a catch-all that governs which transactions are subject to the posting order and to overdraft fees. Whether the general words are limited by the enumerated specifics is the construction question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c051", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The whole posting mechanism turns on \"your available Account balance\", a phrase never defined and used differently across subparagraphs (a) adds available deposits, (b) subtracts unpaid pending authorizations. Whether \"available balance\" means the ledger balance, the Funds Availability Policy balance, or that balance net of pending holds is exactly what a fee dispute would turn on.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.32}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c052", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bank deducts pending authorizations from the available balance \"subject to certain exceptions\", and the exceptions are then said to include an open-ended set of \"certain merchants that frequently request authorization for amounts in excess of the likely transaction amount\". Neither the exceptions nor the merchant category is fixed, so the customer cannot determine his available balance.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.34}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c053", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The category scheme leaves it uncertain which fees fall in category (ii), (iii) or (iv), and \"within categories i, ii, and iii, we post items in order from largest to smallest\" does not say whether items presented on the same day in different categories are ordered by category or by size. The high-to-low rule and the category boundaries are the terms in dispute.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.35}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c054", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Overdraft fees \"may be assessed on items presented for payment that bring your Account into a negative balance\", but \"negative balance\" is not defined and the same paragraph distinguishes the available balance (reduced by pending authorizations) from the balance on which fees are charged. Whether a fee is owed turns on which balance the phrase means and on the permissive \"may\".", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c055", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bank promises \"advance notice\" before changing its processing order but fixes no period, form or method for that notice. What notice suffices, and whether it must satisfy the separate Amendments clause, is left open by the phrase \"advance notice\".", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c056", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The enumerated grounds for refusing an item end with \"(e) we believe is otherwise not properly payable\", a general catch-all sitting against the specific grounds that precede it. Whether \"otherwise not properly payable\" is confined to defects of the enumerated kind is the construction question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c057", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause gives two examples of restrictive legends and then extends to legends \"and the like\", without any criterion for what other notations count as restrictive legends the Bank may disregard. The catch-all is the term needing construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c058", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause has the customer agree in advance never to postdate and denies him any remedy if an early-presented postdated check is paid, without any notice mechanism of the kind postdating rules ordinarily require. Whether that blanket advance waiver of \"any loss to you\" is effective is what would be construed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.19}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c059", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause deems any debit initiated by a party to whom the customer voluntarily gave Account information \"authorized by you\", while Part IV's Unauthorized Transfers section and Electronic Check Conversions provisions give the customer rights over transfers made \"using information from your check\" without permission. The two treatments of the same debit cannot both stand.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c060", "issues": [
   {"issue": "An overdraft is defined here as an advance of funds greater than the amount \"that has become available in accordance with the Bank's Funds Availability Policy\", whereas the Processing Order clauses measure overdrafts against an \"available Account balance\" that is further reduced by pending debit-card authorizations. Which measure determines whether an overdraft — and hence a fee — has occurred cannot be answered from either provision alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.32}
 ]}
]}

file.content:
  "id": "c117",
  "name": "Interest rate inquiry notice",
  "text": "Note: If this disclosure was given to you in connection with an inquiry, the Interest Rate(s) and APY(s) shown are rates that the Bank has offered within the seven (7) most recent Calendar Days, and are accurate as of the date shown on our Retail Rate Sheet. Current rates may be obtained by calling Customer Service at the toll-free number listed on the back of this disclosure."
},
{
  "id": "c118",
  "name": "Non-interest bearing Accounts",
  "text": "TD Convenience Checking, TD Student Checking, TD Simple Checking and Savings Transaction Accounts: These are noninterest bearing Accounts and have no APY."
},
{
  "id": "c119",
  "name": "Variable-rate Accounts",
  "text": "All interest bearing Checking, Savings, and Money Market Accounts: The interest rate and APY may change daily and are adjusted periodically by the Bank based on various economic factors. There is no limit on changes up or down and the rates are subject to change at any time without notice."
},
{
  "id": "c120",
  "name": "Obtaining the disclosed APY",
  "text": "To Obtain the Annual Percentage Yield (“APY”) Disclosed: You must maintain the minimum tier balance in the Account each day in order to obtain the disclosed APY for that particular tier. The APY disclosed assumes the Account remains on deposit for one year at the same interest rate."
},
{
  "id": "c121",
  "name": "TD Relationship Savings — eligible linked accounts",
  "text": "TD Relationship Savings: For personal and certain personal Trust TD Relationship Savings accounts, the interest rate and APY applied will also be determined by whether or not TD Bank has on record an eligible TD Bank account linked to that TD Relationship Savings account. An eligible account is a personal TD Bank Checking, Mortgage, Home Equity, or Credit Card account. 25 Definition of personal and certain personal Trust TD Relationship Savings accounts: Account Eligibility Ownership Type Requirements Requirements TD Relationship In good Individual, Primary or SavingsSM standing Secondary Owner, OR Trust set up with a Social Security Number, or be a Trustee of such a Trust account Eligible accounts you may link: Account Eligibility Ownership Type Requirements Requirements Mortgage*, In good standing Individual, Primary Home Equity or Secondary Line of Credit, Owner Home Equity Loan Credit Card In good standing Individual or Primary Owner Checking In good standing Individual, Primary and, one Deposit, or Secondary Withdrawal, Payment Owner or Transfer transaction during the previous calendar month *Mortgages that we no longer service are not eligible"
},
{
  "id": "c122",
  "name": "TD Relationship Savings — monthly adjustment",
  "text": "On the last Business Day of a calendar month, if you do not have a linked, eligible personal Account (Checking, Mortgage, Home Equity Loan, Home Equity Line of Credit or Credit Card Account), the interest rate and APY applied to your account from the first Business Day of the next calendar month will be adjusted to reflect this change."
},
{
  "id": "c123",
  "name": "TD Relationship Savings — applicable Rate Sheet table",
  "text": "For the current interest rate on your account, please refer to the appropriate table on the accompanying Rate Sheet. 26 Type of TD Relationship Table on Rate Sheet Savings account Qualifying TD Relationship TD Relationship Savings (with Savings accounts with an eligible linked account) TD Bank account linked to it All other TD Relationship Savings TD Relationship Savings accounts (without linked account)"
},
{
  "id": "c124",
  "name": "Non-personal TD Relationship Savings",
  "text": "Non-personal TD Relationship Savings accounts will receive the interest rate and APY applicable to TD Relationship Savings accounts without a linked account."
},
{
  "id": "c125",
  "name": "Linked-account information disclosure",
  "text": "Information regarding your linked account may be made available to any other owner or signer on any of the accounts you have linked."
},
{
  "id": "c126",
  "name": "Trustee linked-account warning",
  "text": "If you choose to link your personal account to an account for which you serve as trustee, either of your accounts may receive a financial benefit, which could be a violation of your fiduciary duties."
},
{
  "id": "c127",
  "name": "TD Growth Money Market — qualification criteria",
  "text": "TD Growth Money Market: For personal and certain personal Trust TD Growth Money Market accounts, the interest rate and APY applied will also be determined by whether your account meets all of the following criteria: a. Whether or not your TD Growth Money Market account qualifies, as defined below: Account Eligibility Ownership Type Requirements Requirements TD Growth In good Individual, Primary Money MarketSM standing or Secondary Owner, OR Trust set up with a Social Security Number, or be a Trustee of such a Trust account b. Whether or not we have on record an eligible, personal TD Bank Checking account linked to your TD Growth Money Market account. Eligible accounts you may link include: Account Eligibility Ownership Type Requirements Requirements Personal In good Individual, Primary or Checking standing Secondary Owner Personal In good Trust set up with Checking (Trust) standing a Social Security Number, or be a Trustee of such a Trust account c. Whether or not your TD Growth Money Market has grown by $50 or more during your current statement cycle. This is determined by comparing the closing balance on your current statement to the closing balance on your previous statement. 27 d. Whether or not you made at least one qualifying transfer into your TD Growth Money Market account during your current statement cycle."
},
{
  "id": "c128",
  "name": "TD Growth Money Market — d.i. qualifying transfer",
  "text": "i. A qualifying transfer is a recurring transfer of any amount from a TD Bank account. Eligible transfers include recurring transfers set up by phone or at a TD Bank Store, or through Online Banking. Transfers set up using ATMs, voice response units, overdraft protection transfers, and sweeps are not eligible."
},
{
  "id": "c129",
  "name": "TD Growth Money Market — d.ii. Immediate transfer",
  "text": "ii. In addition, an Immediate transfer completed through Online Banking will also qualify."
},
{
  "id": "c130",
  "name": "TD Growth Money Market — d.iii. posting period",
  "text": "iii. To be eligible, your qualifying transfer must post during the period starting the first business day and ending the last business day of your current statement cycle. Please be aware of the available balance in your accounts - transferring funds from an account with an insufficient balance may result in an Overdraft and a fee may be charged. Please refer to the Overdraft section for details."
},
{
  "id": "c131",
  "name": "TD Growth Money Market — qualification determination",
  "text": "On the last business day of your statement cycle, we will determine whether you meet the above requirements, and the interest rate and APY applied to your account from the first business day of the next statement cycle will be adjusted, if necessary, to reflect your account qualification status."
},
{
  "id": "c132",
  "name": "Non-personal TD Growth Money Market",
  "text": "Non-personal TD Growth Money Market accounts will receive the interest rate and APY applicable to TD Growth Money Market accounts without qualifying activity."
},
{
  "id": "c133",
  "name": "TD Growth linked-account information disclosure",
  "text": "Information regarding your linked account may be made available to any other owner or signer on any of the accounts you have linked."
},
{
  "id": "c134",
  "name": "TD Growth trustee linked-account warning",
  "text": "If you choose to link your personal account to an account for which you serve as trustee, either of your accounts may receive a financial benefit, which could be a violation of your fiduciary duties."
},
{
  "id": "c135",
  "name": "Fixed Rate CDs",
  "text": "Fixed Rate CDs: The interest rate and APY are fixed for the term of the certificate and may only be changed at maturity."
},
{
  "id": "c136",
  "name": "Step Rate CD",
  "text": "Step Rate CD: Three (3) and five (5) year terms are available. The APY will increase every year on the anniversary of the Account open date. At maturity, the Step Rate CD will renew to a one (1) year term."
},
{
  "id": "c137",
  "name": "2A. TD Relationship Checking, TD Relationship Savings and Private High Yield Savings Accounts",
  "text": "2A. TD Relationship Checking, TD Relationship Savings and Private High Yield Savings Accounts: The Chart which follows indicates the balance tier levels used to determine the variable interest rate and APY being applied to your Account. The interest rate and annual percentage yield for the appropriate tier will be paid on the full balance in the Account. Balance Tier Structure: $ 0.01 – $ 999.99 $ 50,000.00 – $ 99,999.99 $ 1,000.00 – $ 9,999.99 $ 100,000.00 – $249,999.99 $10,000.00 – $24,999.99 $ 250,000.00 – $499,999.99 $25,000.00 – $49,999.99 $ 500,000.00 – $999,999.99 $1,000,000.00+"
},
{
  "id": "c138",
  "name": "2B. TD Growth Money Market",
  "text": "2B. TD Growth Money Market: The Chart below indicates the balance tier levels used to determine the variable interest rate and APY being applied to your Account. The interest rate and annual percentage yield for the appropriate tier will be paid on the full balance in the Account. Balance Tier Structure: $ 0.01 – $ 999.99 $ 10,000.00 – $ 24,999.99 $1,000.00 – $1,999.99 $ 25,000.00 – $ 49,999.99 $2,000.00 – $4,999.99 $ 50,000.00 – $ 99,999.99 $5,000.00 – $9,999.99 $100,000.00 – $249,999.99 $250,000.00+"
},
{
  "id": "c139",
  "name": "2C. TD Premier Checking",
  "text": "2C. TD Premier Checking: The Chart below indicates the balance tier levels used to determine the variable interest rate and APY being applied to your Account. The interest rate and annual percentage yield for the appropriate tier will be paid on the full balance in the Account. Balance Tier Structure: $ 0.01 – $ 2,499.99 $ 50,000.00 – $249,999.99 $2,500.00 – $49,999.99 $250,000.00+"
},
{
  "id": "c140",
  "name": "2D. Private Tiered Checking Account",
  "text": "2D. Private Tiered Checking Account: The Chart below indicates the balance tier levels used to determine the variable interest rate and APY being applied to your Account. The interest rate and annual percentage yield for the appropriate tier will be paid on the full balance in the Account. Balance Tier Structure: $ 0.01 – $ 9,999.99 $ 25,000.00 – $249,999.99 $10,000.00 – $24,999.99 $250,000.00 – $499,999.99 $500,000.00+"
},
{
  "id": "c141",
  "name": "2E. Health Savings Account",
  "text": "2E. Health Savings Account: The Chart on page 31 indicates the balance tier levels used to determine the variable interest rate and APY being applied to your Account. The interest rate and annual percentage yield for the appropriate tier will be paid on the full balance in the Account. 29 Balance Tier Structure: $ 0.01 – $2,499.99 $10,000.00 – $24,999.99 $2,500.00 – $9,999.99 $25,000.00 – $49,999.99 $50,000.00+"
},
{
  "id": "c142",
  "name": "2F(i). Early Withdrawal Penalties",
  "text": "2F. NOTICE: Applicable to Certificates of Deposit ONLY: (i) Early Withdrawal Penalties: No part of the principal may be withdrawn prior to maturity without the Bank’s consent. No withdrawals will be permitted during the first seven (7) days of the CD term. If the Bank does allow an early withdrawal, the following penalties will apply: CD Term Penalty (including Basic, No Catch and IRA Add-Vantage CDs) 7 – 89 days All interest 90 days < 1 year 3 months’ interest 1 year < 2 years 6 months’ interest 2 years + 9 months’ interest Step Rate CD Term Penalty 3 years 9 months interest 5 years 12 months interest In certain circumstances, such as the death or incompetence of an owner of the CD, the penalty may be waived. In no circumstances can the amount withdrawn bring the balance to below the Minimum to Open, as disclosed in the accompanying Account Maintenance Information grid."
},
{
  "id": "c143",
  "name": "Step Rate CD — anniversary grace period",
  "text": "Step Rate CD: Partial and full withdrawals may be made without penalty during a ten (10) day grace period that begins on each anniversary of the account opening date."
},
{
  "id": "c144",
  "name": "“No Catch” CD withdrawals",
  "text": "“No Catch” CD: At no cost to you, you will have the option to withdraw principal funds without penalty once during the term of the CD. Therefore, if you choose to withdraw principal funds, there will be no penalty for that withdrawal. More than one withdrawal of principal during the term of this CD may result in a penalty. The interest rate and APY remain the same for the term. No withdrawals will be permitted during the first seven (7) days of the CD term."
},
{
  "id": "c145",
  "name": "2F(ii). Withdrawal of Interest Prior To Maturity",
  "text": "(ii) Withdrawal of Interest Prior To Maturity: The APY disclosed assumes interest and principal will remain on deposit until maturity. A withdrawal will reduce earnings. For CDs of less than one (1) year, the APY assumes the CD remains on deposit for one (1) year at the current rate."
},
{
  "id": "c146",
  "name": "2F(iii). Renewal Policies",
  "text": "(iii) Renewal Policies: Unless otherwise noted, CDs will automatically renew to the same term at maturity. At maturity, the Step Rate CD will renew to a one (1) year CD."
},
{
  "id": "c147",
  "name": "CD maturity grace period",
  "text": "At maturity you will have ten (10) Calendar Days after the maturity date to withdraw the funds without penalty. Interest not withdrawn will be converted to principal upon the renewal of the certificate."
},
{
  "id": "c148",
  "name": "2F(iv). Interest Computation",
  "text": "(iv) Interest Computation: Interest is accrued on all deposits as of the day the Account is opened on a 365/365-day basis (366/366-day basis during a leap year), and is compounded monthly on the cycle date. The APY for the Account assumes that interest will remain on deposit until maturity; a withdrawal will reduce earnings. The daily balance method is used to calculate the interest on the Account. This method applies a daily periodic rate to the principal in the Account each day. Interest is credited monthly for all CDs."
},
{
  "id": "c149",
  "name": "3. Frequency of Compounding and Crediting of Interest",
  "text": "3. Frequency of Compounding and Crediting of Interest (Applicable to All Interest Bearing Accounts): With the exception of Holiday Club and Club Saver Accounts, the Bank compounds interest monthly. Interest is credited on a monthly basis. For Holiday Club and Club Saver Accounts, the Bank compounds interest daily and credits the interest at maturity. If you or we close your interest bearing Account before the date of interest posting, accrued interest in the amount of $10 or more will be paid. Accrued interest in an amount under $10 will not be paid except at the discretion of the Bank."
},
{
  "id": "c150",
  "name": "4(i). To Open Accounts",
  "text": "4. Minimum Balance Requirements (All Accounts): (i) To Open Accounts: To open an Account, you must deposit the amount shown in the accompanying Account Maintenance Information grid."
},
{
  "id": "c151",
  "name": "4(ii). To Avoid Imposition of Monthly Maintenance Fees",
  "text": "(ii) To Avoid Imposition of Monthly Maintenance Fees: To avoid the imposition of monthly maintenance fees, you must maintain the minimum required daily balance specified for your type of Account for that particular monthly cycle. See the accompanying Account Maintenance Information grid for your type Account."
},
{
  "id": "c152",
  "name": "4(iii). TD Simple Savings waiver",
  "text": "(iii) TD Simple Savings: The monthly maintenance fee for TD Simple Savings accounts will be waived in each service charge cycle (a monthly period based on your statement date) that the account meets all of the criteria specified below. This waiver is only available for 12 months from the date you open your account, or 12 months from the date when you switch your account to TD Simple Savings."
},
{
  "id": "c153",
  "name": "TD Simple Savings — a. qualifying account",
  "text": "a. Your TD Simple Savings account must qualify, as defined below: Account Eligibility Ownership Type Requirements Requirements TD Simple In good Individual, Primary or SavingsSM standing Secondary Owner, OR Trust set up with a Social Security Number, or be a Trustee of such a Trust account"
},
{
  "id": "c154",
  "name": "TD Simple Savings — b. linked Checking account",
  "text": "b. We must have on record an eligible, personal TD Bank Checking account linked to your TD Simple Savings account. Eligible accounts you may link include: Account Eligibility Ownership Type Requirements Requirements Personal In good Individual, Primary or Checking standing Secondary Owner Personal In good Trust set up with a Checking (Trust) standing Social Security Number, or be a Trustee of such a Trust account"
},
{
  "id": "c155",
  "name": "TD Simple Savings — c. qualifying transfer requirement",
  "text": "c. There must have been at least one qualifying transfer into your TD Simple Savings account."
},
{
  "id": "c156",
  "name": "TD Simple Savings — c.i. qualifying transfer",
  "text": "i. A qualifying transfer is a recurring transfer of at least $25 from a TD Bank account. Eligible transfers include recurring transfers set up by phone or at a TD Bank Store, or through Online Banking. Transfers set up using ATMs, voice response units, overdraft protection transfers, and sweeps are not eligible."
},
{
  "id": "c157",
  "name": "TD Simple Savings — c.ii. Immediate transfer",
  "text": "ii. In addition, an Immediate transfer completed through Online Banking will also qualify."
},
{
  "id": "c158",
  "name": "TD Simple Savings — c.iii. posting period",
  "text": "iii. To be eligible, your qualifying transfer must post during the period starting the last business day of your previous service charge cycle and ending the second-to-last business day of your current service charge cycle (See example in chart below). Please be aware of the available balance in your accounts – transferring funds from an account with an insufficient balance may result in an Overdraft and a fee may be charged. Please refer to the Overdraft section for details"
},
{
  "id": "c159",
  "name": "TD Simple Savings — qualification determination",
  "text": "We will determine whether your account qualifies for this monthly maintenance fee waiver on the second-to-last business day of your current service charge cycle."
},
{
  "id": "c160",
  "name": "4(iv). Monthly Maintenance Fee Discount",
  "text": "(iv) Monthly Maintenance Fee Discount: For all personal checking, savings, money market and health savings accounts that are charged a monthly maintenance fee, except for Private Banking Accounts, the monthly fee will be reduced by $1.00 when you choose to stop receiving printed and mailed statements and switch to online statements only. The fee reduction is not applicable to passbook accounts."
},
{
  "id": "c161",
  "name": "5. Balance Computation Method",
  "text": "5. Balance Computation Method: We use the daily balance method to calculate interest on your Account. This method applies a periodic rate to the principal in the Account each day."
},
{
  "id": "c162",
  "name": "6. Accrual of Interest",
  "text": "6. Accrual of Interest: For all deposit accounts (except CDs), interest begins to accrue no later than the Business Day we receive credit for the deposit of non-cash items (for example, checks)."
},
{
  "id": "c163",
  "name": "7. Fees & Charges",
  "text": "7. Fees & Charges: Monthly maintenance fees are shown in the accompanying Account Maintenance Information grid. You agree to pay all fees applicable to the Account including those detailed in the Personal Fee Schedule. You will be notified at least thirty (30) days in advance of any changes to these fees."
},
{
  "id": "c164",
  "name": "8. Account Opening Bonus Promotions — cash bonus",
  "text": "8. Account Opening Bonus Promotions: From time to time, we may offer cash bonus promotions for opening a new non-interest bearing checking account with an initial deposit of $100 or more. If we are offering such a promotion, and if you open a new non-interest bearing checking account with an initial deposit of at least $100 during the promotional period, you will receive a $25 cash bonus when you open the account. This bonus will be credited to your checking account on the business day it is opened. These promotions cannot be combined with any other offer and are limited to one bonus per Customer. The value of this bonus may be reported to the Internal Revenue Service."
},
{
  "id": "c165",
  "name": "8. Account Opening Bonus Promotions — Visa Gift Card bonus",
  "text": "In addition, from time to time, we may offer a TD Bank Visa® Gift Card bonus promotion for opening a new non-interest bearing checking account with an initial deposit of $250 or more. If we are offering such a promotion, and if you open a new non-interest bearing checking account with an initial deposit of at least $250 during the promotional period, you will receive a $25 TD Bank Visa® Gift Card bonus when you open the account. This bonus will be provided on the business day it is opened. These promotions cannot be combined with any other offer and are limited to one bonus per Customer. The value of this bonus may be reported to the Internal Revenue Service."
},
{
  "id": "c166",
  "name": "8. Account Opening Bonus Promotions — Direct Deposit bonus",
  "text": "Also, from time to time, we may offer cash bonus promotions for enrolling in Direct Deposit in conjunction with opening a new non-interest bearing checking account with an initial deposit of $100 or more. If we are offering such a promotion, and if you open a new non-interest bearing checking account with an initial deposit of at least $100 and enroll in Direct Deposit on the spot during the promotional period, you will receive a $25 cash bonus when you open the account. This bonus will be credited to your checking account on the business day it is opened. These promotions cannot be combined with any other offer and are limited to one bonus per Customer. The value of this bonus may be reported to the Internal Revenue Service."
},
{
  "id": "c167",
  "name": "9. Promotional CD Interest Rates — eligibility",
  "text": "9. Promotional CD Interest Rates: From time to time, we may offer Promotional CD interest rates which may have different account opening requirements than our non-promotional (Basic) CD terms. These requirements will be disclosed on the Retail Deposit Rate Sheet. If we are offering such a promotion and you are opening a new account, you must deposit the required initial minimum balance to open the account in money not already on deposit at TD Bank to qualify. If we are offering such a promotion and you have a renewing CD, you may be eligible for the promotional rate by making a deposit of new to bank money to the renewing CD that is equal to or greater than the new account minimum balance requirement. Maximum deposit limits may apply."
},
{
  "id": "c168",
  "name": "9. Promotional CD Interest Rates — renewal",
  "text": "Promotional CDs will automatically renew at maturity to the same term at the non-promotional (Basic) CD interest rate and APY in effect at the time of renewal unless we notify you otherwise. Promotional CD interest rates and/or Special Offers apply only until the promotional CD’s first maturity date."
},
{
  "id": "c169",
  "name": "10. Grand Opening Bonus CD Rate — eligibility",
  "text": "10. Grand Opening Bonus CD Rate: We may offer a special Grand Opening Bonus CD rate at new TD Bank Store locations. If we are offering such a promotion, you must deposit the required initial minimum balance to open the account in money not already on deposit at TD Bank to qualify. The maximum deposit is $1,000,000. The offer is valid for new CD accounts only and does not include IRA CDs. A TD Bank personal checking account is required."
},
{
  "id": "c170",
  "name": "10. Grand Opening Bonus CD Rate — renewal",
  "text": "Grand Opening Bonus CDs will renew at maturity to the same term at the non-promotional (Basic) CD interest rate and APY in effect at the time of renewal unless we notify you otherwise. Grand Opening Bonus CD interest rate and/ or Special Offers apply to the initial CD term only."
},
{
  "id": "c171",
  "name": "11. Additional Deposits (“IRA Add-Vantage CD” only)",
  "text": "11. Additional Deposits (“IRA Add-Vantage CD” only): You may make additional deposits of not less than $500.00 per deposit at any time during the term up to a maximum of $250,000 in additional deposits."
},
{
  "id": "c172",
  "name": "Part III — Funds Availability Policy scope",
  "text": "Part III: Funds Availability Policy Your ability to withdraw funds you have deposited at the Bank will be determined according to this policy."
},
{
  "id": "c173",
  "name": "Funds Availability Policy — covered Accounts",
  "text": "This disclosure applies to all transaction accounts such as Checking and Interest Bearing Checking Accounts, and to Money Market, Savings, and Time Accounts."
},
{
  "id": "c174",
  "name": "Funds Availability Policy — general availability",
  "text": "The Bank’s general policy is to make funds from your deposits available to you no later than the first (1st) Business Day after the day we receive your deposit. Electronic direct deposits and wire transfers will be available on the day we receive the deposit. Once they are available, you can withdraw the funds in cash and we will use the funds to pay checks that you have written."
},
{
  "id": "c175",
  "name": "Determining the Availability of a Deposit — cutoff time",
  "text": "Determining the Availability of a Deposit To determine the availability of your deposits, every day is a Business Day, except Saturdays, Sundays and federal holidays. On Business Days that we are open, the earliest time that we stop accepting deposits in our Stores for same-day credit is 8pm Thus, if you make a deposit with a bank teller before 8pm on a Business Day that we are open, we will consider that day to be the day of your deposit. However, if you make a deposit after 8pm or on a day we are not open, we will consider that the deposit was made on the next Business Day we are open."
},
{
  "id": "c176",
  "name": "Determining availability — mailed and night deposits",
  "text": "If you mail funds to us, the funds are considered deposited on the Business Day we receive them. Funds deposited in a night depository or Store lockbox are considered deposited on the next Business Day the Bank or Store lockbox is open."
},
{
  "id": "c177",
  "name": "Determining availability — ATM deposits",
  "text": "If you make a deposit at a Bank ATM before 8pm on a Business Day that we are open, we will consider that day to be the day of your deposit. However, if you make a deposit at a Bank ATM after 8pm or on a day we are not open, we will consider that the deposit was made on the next Business Day we are open. Funds from any deposits (cash or checks) made at ATMs we do not own or operate may not be available until the fifth (5th) Business Day after the day of your deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c178",
  "name": "Same Day Availability",
  "text": "Same Day Availability Funds from the following deposits are available on the same day they are deposited: • Cash deposits made at the Bank’s teller station; • Funds received for deposit by an electronic payment (including ACH credits and transfers); • Wire transfers; • $100.00 from non-cash deposits made at the Bank’s teller station; • $100.00 from deposits made at the Bank’s ATM (for accounts opened longer than 90 days)."
},
{
  "id": "c179",
  "name": "Longer Delays May Apply — ordinary check delay",
  "text": "Longer Delays May Apply In some cases, we will not make all the funds that you deposit by check available at the times shown in this Policy. Depending on the type of check you deposit, funds may not be available until the second (2nd) Business Day after the day of your deposit. The first $200 of your deposit, however, will be available no later than the first (1st) Business Day after the day of your deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c180",
  "name": "Longer Delays May Apply — notice",
  "text": "If we are not going to make all of the funds from your deposit available on the first (1st) Business Day, we will notify you at the time you make your deposit. We will also tell you when the funds will be available. If your deposit is not made directly to one of our 35 employees, or if we decide to take this action after you have left the premises, we will mail you the notice by the day after we receive your deposit. If you will need the funds from a deposit right away, you should ask us when the funds will be available."
},
{
  "id": "c181",
  "name": "Longer Delays May Apply — extended-delay circumstances",
  "text": "In addition, funds deposited by check may be delayed for a longer period under the following circumstances: • you deposit checks totaling more than $5,000 on any one day (Note: The first $200 will be made available no later than the first (1st) Business Day after the day of your deposit); • we believe a check you deposited will not be paid; • you re-deposit a check that has been returned unpaid; • you have overdrawn your Account repeatedly, or would have overdrawn your account if checks had been honored in the last six (6) months; • there is an emergency, such as failure of communications or computer equipment. (Note: The first $200 will be made available no later than the first (1st) Business Day after the day of your deposit). We will notify you if we delay your ability to withdraw funds for any of these reasons, and we will tell you when the funds will be available. They will generally be available no later than the seventh (7th) Business Day after the day of your deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c182",
  "name": "Special Rules For New Accounts — applicability",
  "text": "Special Rules For New Accounts If you are a new Customer, the following special rules may apply during the first thirty (30) days your account is open."
},
{
  "id": "c183",
  "name": "New Accounts — cash, direct deposits and wires",
  "text": "Funds from in-Store cash deposits, electronic direct deposits, and wire transfers to your Account will be available on the day we receive the deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c184",
  "name": "New Accounts — first $100 in-Store non-cash deposits",
  "text": "The first $100 of your daily in-Store non-cash deposits will be available to you on the day we receive the deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c185",
  "name": "New Accounts — first $5,000 of specified checks",
  "text": "Funds from the first $5,000 of a day’s total deposits of cashier’s, certified, teller’s, traveler’s, and federal, state, and local government checks will be available on the first (1st) Business Day after the day of your deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c186",
  "name": "New Accounts — excess and other checks",
  "text": "The excess over $5,000 and funds from all other check deposits will be available no later than the seventh (7th) Business Day after the day of your deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c187",
  "name": "New Customers using an ATM — applicability",
  "text": "For new Customers using an ATM, the following additional special rules may apply during the first ninety (90) days your account is open."
},
{
  "id": "c188",
  "name": "New Customers — TD Bank ATM deposits",
  "text": "Cash deposits and the first $100 of a check deposit made at a TD Bank ATM will be available to you on the first (1st) business day after the day of your deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c189",
  "name": "New Customers — non-TD ATM cash deposits",
  "text": "Cash deposits made at an ATM the Bank does not own or operate will be available no later than the fifth (5th) business day after the day of your deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c190",
  "name": "New Customers — non-TD ATM check deposits",
  "text": "Check deposits made at an ATM the Bank does not own or operate will be available no later than the seventh (7th) business day after the day of your deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c191",
  "name": "Holds on Other Funds",
  "text": "Holds on Other Funds If we accept for deposit or we cash a check that is drawn on another bank, we may make funds from the deposit available for withdrawal immediately, but delay your availability to withdraw a corresponding amount of funds that you have on deposit in another Account with us. The funds in the other Account would then not be available for withdrawal in accordance with the time periods that are described in this policy."
},
{
  "id": "c192",
  "name": "Non-U.S. Financial Institutions",
  "text": "Non-U.S. Financial Institutions We reserve the right to send any checks drawn on a foreign financial institution (including Canadian financial institutions) for collection. For each item sent, we will assess a collection charge plus any collection fees charged to us by other financial institutions which process the item as listed in our most recent Personal Fee Schedule. While the funds represented by checks that are sent for collection are generally available within thirty (30) Calendar Days or subject to payment by the Drawee bank, items sent for collection will be credited to your Account in U.S. dollars, with the amount of U.S. dollars credited calculated using our applicable exchange rate that is in effect on the date when we credit the funds to your Account and not when the deposit is made. If we do not enter any item (Canadian only) for collection, the funds will be available no later than the third (3rd) Business Day after the day of deposit."
},
{
  "id": "c193",
  "name": "Checks or Other Items Returned Subsequent to Funds Being Made Available",
  "text": "Checks or Other Items Returned Subsequent to Funds Being Made Available If a check or other item you deposited to your Account is returned to us unpaid after the funds have been made available to you, the amount of the check or other item will be deducted from your Account. If there are insufficient funds in your Account, we reserve the right to demand payment directly from you and to charge you for the overdraft as posted in our most recent Personal Fee Schedule."
},
{
  "id": "c194",
  "name": "Endorsements",
  "text": "Endorsements Endorsements on items deposited to your Account are restricted, under federal law, to the first 1.5 inches of the back of the check. The remaining portion of the check is reserved for endorsements by banks. Your endorsement should contain your signature, the words “For Deposit Only,” and your Account number. Improper endorsements may delay the check collection process and the subsequent crediting and availability of funds. While we may accept non-conforming endorsements, you agree you will be responsible for any losses."
},
{
  "id": "c195",
  "name": "Part IV — Electronic Funds Transfers Disclosure",
  "text": "Part IV: Electronic Funds Transfers Disclosure The Electronic Funds Transfers (“EFT”) we are capable of handling are indicated below. Some of these may not apply to your Account. Please read this disclosure carefully because it tells you your rights and obligations for these transactions. You should keep this notice for future reference."
},
{
  "id": "c196",
  "name": "EFT country restrictions",
  "text": "Use of your ATM or Visa Debit Card may be restricted in certain countries due to security risks."
},
{
  "id": "c197",
  "name": "Card cancellation for inactivity",
  "text": "For security purposes, your card may be cancelled after 13 months of inactivity, except for Health Savings Account Debit Cards, which may be cancelled after 36 months of inactivity."
},
{
  "id": "c198",
  "name": "Direct Deposits",
  "text": "Direct Deposits You may make arrangements for certain direct deposits to be accepted into your Checking, Savings or Money Market Deposit Accounts."
},
{
  "id": "c199",
  "name": "Pre-authorized Withdrawals",
  "text": "Pre-authorized Withdrawals You may make arrangements to pay certain recurring bills from your Checking, Statement Savings or Statement Money Market Deposit Accounts."
},
{
  "id": "c200",
  "name": "Telephone Transfers",
  "text": "Telephone Transfers You may make arrangements to have telephone transfers between eligible Checking, Statement Savings or Statement Money Market Deposit Accounts through our telephone banking system."
},
{
  "id": "c201",
  "name": "Electronic Check Conversions",
  "text": "Electronic Check Conversions Some Point-of-Purchase terminals may provide you the option of initiating a one-time automatic debit from your Account by authorizing the merchant to obtain the necessary information from a check drawn on your deposit account. A check used in this way is treated as an EFT and is not a negotiable instrument in its own right. The check cannot be subsequently used and should be voided."
},
{
  "id": "c202",
  "name": "One-time electronic check payments",
  "text": "You may authorize a merchant or other payee to make a onetime electronic payment from your Checking Account using information from your check to: (i) Pay for purchases (ii) Pay bills"
},
{
  "id": "c203",
  "name": "ATM Transaction Types",
  "text": "ATM Transaction Types You may access your Account(s) by ATM using your ATM card or Visa Debit Card and Personal Identification Number (PIN) to: • make deposits to Checking, Statement Savings, and Statement Money Market Accounts at TD Bank ATMs; 38 • get cash withdrawals and/or transfer funds from and between Checking, Statement Savings, and Statement Money Market Accounts linked to your card; • make envelope-free deposits at many TD Bank ATMs; • get information about the Account balance(s) in the Checking, Statement Savings, and/or Statement Money Market Account(s) linked to your card. Note: Some of these services may not be available at all terminals."
},
{
  "id": "c204",
  "name": "Visa Debit Card Transaction Types",
  "text": "Visa Debit Card Transaction Types In addition to the ATM transaction types listed above, with your Visa Debit Card, you may: • purchase goods online, via phone or in person, or pay for services wherever Visa Debit Cards are accepted; • get cash from a merchant, if the merchant permits, or from a participating financial institution."
},
{
  "id": "c205",
  "name": "Visa authorization limitation",
  "text": "Note: If a merchant receives authorization for a purchase, TD Bank cannot return that transaction unpaid even if your account is not in good standing."
},
{
  "id": "c206",
  "name": "Visa Debit Card Limits",
  "text": "Visa Debit Card Limits The standard daily limits (per card) are: • ATM cash withdrawals – $750; • POS (PIN) transactions – $2,000; • Visa signature transactions and Visa cash advances – $5,000 each."
},
