{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c061", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause says a fee is charged \"for each transaction that overdraws your account\" only if the \"negative available balance exceeds $5 at the end of the day\", while the Processing Order clause states that overdraft fees may be assessed on any item that brings the Account into a negative balance and on every subsequent item while it stays negative. The two rules for when a fee is earned cannot both be applied to the same day's items.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c062", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause obliges the customer to pay \"all of our costs of collecting an overdraft ... includ[ing] ... our legal fees and expenses\", whereas the \"If You Owe Us Money\" clause limits recovery to \"court costs and reasonable attorneys' fees as awarded by the court\". Which measure of fees applies to a suit to collect an overdraft is unresolved between them.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.23}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c063", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c064", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause repeats three times that the fee may be charged when the Account \"remains in overdrawn status for ten (10) consecutive Business Days\" without saying whether the fee is charged once or recurs for each further ten-day period, and \"overdrawn status\" is not defined. Whether a second or third sustained fee is authorized is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.21}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c065", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Closure is triggered either at sixty Calendar Days or at \"such earlier time that we determine that the overdraft balance is uncollectible\", a determination committed entirely to the Bank with no standard. The uncollectibility trigger is what a court would have to construe.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c066", "issues": [
   {"issue": "A stop payment request is effective only if it \"precisely identif[ies] the Account number, check number, date and amount of the item, and the payee\", a strict-accuracy requirement with no tolerance for an immaterial error. Whether \"precisely\" defeats a request describing the item with substantial accuracy is the construction question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c067", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause makes an oral stop payment effective for a full year \"[r]egardless of whether\" it was made orally or in writing, but then requires written requests to be on a Bank-supplied form and makes the customer responsible for the accuracy of the written confirmation. Whether an oral request survives an inaccurate or unreturned confirmation is not answered.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c068", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c069", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause both says \"reasonable time depends on the circumstances\" and fixes a safe harbour ending the next Business Day, leaving unclear whether the safe harbour is the only measure or merely one sufficient case. \"Reasonable time\" is the term carrying the Bank's whole exposure for paying over a stop order.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.25}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c070", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c071", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause promises payment of the customer's established loss \"up to the face amount of the check\" for payment over a stop order, but the Limited Liability clause caps all recovery at the total fees paid in the preceding three months and bars liability absent bad faith. The two limits on the same claim cannot both control.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c072", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bank will attempt a stop only if the customer \"certif[ies] to our satisfaction\" that the item was lost, stolen or destroyed, a wholly subjective trigger, and \"other similar item\" is undefined alongside cashier's and teller's checks. Both phrases leave the Bank's duty indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.13}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c073", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c074", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c075", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c076", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c077", "issues": [
   {"issue": "New fee rules \"will take effect after the Change Date\" while the parallel interest rule takes effect \"on the day\" of the change, so it is unclear whether fees assessed on the Change Date itself, or cycle-end fees for a period spanning the change, follow the old or new rules. \"After the Change Date\" is the phrase to construe.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c078", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c079", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The first sentence limits recognition of an attorney-in-fact to the period before written or actual notice of revocation, but the last sentence disclaims liability for \"any payment made to, or at the direction of, a person holding a power of attorney\" without that limit. Whether the disclaimer covers payments after notice of revocation is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c080", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"We need not honor any claim against or involving an Account\" absent a court order is then applied to \"any person asserting any rights or interest regarding an Account, including you\", which on its face lets the Bank refuse the depositor's own demand for his funds. The word \"claim\" and the inclusion of the depositor are what would be construed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c081", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Suspension may follow any claim, dispute or proceeding the Bank \"reasonably believe[s] involves you\", on \"any Account which we believe to be affected\", and is expressly permitted even when due to \"inadvertence, error because of similarity of the names of depositors, or other mistake\". The belief-based trigger has no ascertainable limit and no stated duration.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c082", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bank may comply with any legal process \"which we believe to be valid, without any liability from us to you\", making the Bank's own belief the measure of a customer's rights against it. Whether that belief must be reasonable or in good faith is not stated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c083", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bank is \"entitled to a processing fee\" on receipt of legal process without any amount, cap or cross-reference, while the Agreement elsewhere promises that charges are those \"listed on the Personal Fee Schedule and Account Maintenance Information grid\". What the customer has agreed to pay cannot be determined from the two read together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c084", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The customer agrees the Bank may comply with legal process \"irrespective of how and/or where it was received even if the law requires any particular method of service\", an advance agreement to disregard statutory service requirements. Whether a depositor can contract away the service protections of process directed at his funds is the question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c085", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This clause requires indemnity for legal actions \"including any interpleader action we commence involving you or your Account\", yet the general Indemnity clause states that \"[t]his indemnification does not apply to claims that you may assert against us\". Whether the customer must indemnify the Bank in litigation the Bank brings against him cannot be settled from either clause alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c086", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Upon initiation of an interpleader action, we will be relieved and discharged of all further duties and obligations\" does not say whether the discharge is confined to the disputed funds or extends to every duty the Bank owes under the Agreement. The scope of \"all further duties and obligations\" is the defect.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.25}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c087", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Recovery here is limited to \"court costs and reasonable attorneys' fees as awarded by the court and as permitted by law\", while the Overdrafts clause makes the customer liable for \"all of our costs of collecting an overdraft ... to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law\", including legal fees. Which applies to a suit over an overdraft is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c088", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Set-off is available for \"any debt you owe us that is in default\", but the Agreement's Default clause defines default only in terms of the Account and includes triggers resting on the Bank's \"sole discretion\" as to your \"condition or affairs\". Whether a debt is \"in default\" for set-off purposes therefore depends on a clause written for a different purpose.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.23}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c089", "issues": [
   {"issue": "A hold may be placed whenever the Bank \"ha[s] a claim against you or pending exercise of our right of set-off\", with no stated duration, notice or release condition. The open-ended hold power is what a court would have to construe.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
