 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c240", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c241", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bank \"must hear from you no later than sixty (60) Calendar Days after we sent you the FIRST statement on which the problem or error appeared\", whereas the Part I Periodic Statement clause bars claims not reported within thirty Calendar Days of mailing. For an electronic transfer appearing on a statement the two notice periods conflict.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c242", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"[W]e may not provisionally credit your Account\" if a written complaint is not received within ten Business Days, leaving it uncertain whether the failure forfeits provisional credit or merely permits the Bank to withhold it, and whether it affects the underlying claim. \"May not\" is the phrase carrying the consequence.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c243", "issues": [
   {"issue": "After setting out a forty-five day and a ninety day extended investigation period, the clause says \"[i]f we decide to do this, we will credit your Account\", without identifying which of the two extensions triggers the provisional credit obligation. The antecedent of \"this\" determines when the customer gets his money.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.23}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c244", "issues": []},
