 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c249", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The obligation falls on \"all new Depositors\", a capitalized term never defined and distinguished from the \"Existing Depositors\" of the next subparagraph only by the September 1, 2011 date. Who is a new as opposed to an existing Depositor is not stated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.19}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c250", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Existing Depositors\" may keep using their own containers, while the preceding subparagraph requires \"all new Depositors\" to use Bank-supplied disposable bags; neither term is defined and the classes are not exhaustive. A depositor who resumes the service after a gap falls into neither category.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c251", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c252", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c253", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c254", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause deems the Carrier \"your exclusive agent when items are in transit\" even where, by its own first sentence, \"[w]e may arrange for and pay for a Carrier to collect deposits from you\". Whether a carrier selected, engaged and paid by the Bank can be the customer's exclusive agent is the question the clause creates.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c255", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Liability here is excluded except for loss \"directly caused by our negligence or willful misconduct\", while the Part I Limited Liability clause excludes all liability \"unless we have acted in bad faith\" and caps damages at three months' fees. The Agreement thus states two different standards of care for the same Bank.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.21}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c256", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c257", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"[T]he determination of our employee is conclusive as to the contents of the bags\" makes the Bank the final judge of the amount deposited, while the next clause promises \"ordinary care and ... reasonable commercial standards\" in processing the bags. A conclusive determination leaves no room to test whether that care was exercised.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c258", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This allows \"up to two Business Days following the day the bag is received\" to count and credit the deposit, while the Funds Availability Policy provides that funds deposited in a night depository are considered deposited on the next Business Day the Bank is open and available on that schedule. The two dating and crediting rules conflict, and this clause also says the Policy \"applies to all deposits\".", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c259", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The undertaking to \"use ordinary care and adhere to the reasonable commercial standards of the banking business\" sits against the preceding clause making the Bank employee's count \"conclusive as to the contents of the bags\" and the Liability of Bank clause disclaiming responsibility for loss \"resulting from any cause whatsoever\". Whether the ordinary care promise is enforceable at all depends on reading the three together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.21}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c260", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Fees may be changed \"in the manner specified in the Deposit Account Agreement\", but that Agreement contains two different change-notice rules — the Amendments clause's notice \"as we determine is appropriate\" and Part II §7's thirty days' advance notice of fee changes. The cross-reference does not identify which manner is meant.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c261", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c262", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This declares the Night Depository Agreement \"the entire agreement between you and us with respect to the use of the night depository service\", while the introduction to the instrument states that \"[t]his Agreement consists of Parts I-VI\" together with the Rate Sheets, Fee Schedules and grids. Whether Part VI stands alone or is one part of a single integrated contract is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c263", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Part VI controls over \"any provision of the Deposit Account Agreement relative to the night depository service\", but no criterion is given for when a general provision — the Limited Liability clause, the Funds Availability Policy, the Amendments clause — is \"relative to\" that service. The reach of the priority rule is what would be construed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.23}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c264", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Part VI is governed by \"the state laws that apply to your primary deposit account\", a term used nowhere else and undefined, whereas the Part I Governing Law clause looks to the jurisdiction of the Store where the Account was opened. Which law governs, and which account is \"primary\" for a customer with several, is not answerable from the text.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
 ]}
]}

